=======================================================================
             The Optical Gravitational Lensing Experiment.
           Gaia South Ecliptic Pole Field as Seen by OGLE-IV.
                          Variable Stars

  I. Soszynski, A. Udalski, R. Poleski, S. Kozlowski, L. Wyrzykowski,
P. Pietrukowicz, M.K. Szymanski, M. Kubiak, G. Pietrzynski, K. Ulaczyk,
                           & J. Skowron

=======================================================================
soszynsk@astrouw.edu.pl

This directory contains the catalog of variable stars in the Gaia South
Ecliptic Pole field.

The directory structure is as follows:

README            - this file

list.dat          - list of variable stars with their parameters

remarks.txt       - remarks on selected objects

phot/I/           - I-band photometry of individual objects
phot/V/           - V-band photometry of individual objects
phot.tar.gz       - gzipped phot/ directory

fcharts/          - finding charts of individual objects

ogle-sep-varstars.fits - FITS table version version of the list.dat file

Format of the file list.dat:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
 Bytes  Format Units   Description
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
  1- 15  A15   ---     OGLE-IV star's ID
 18- 19  I2    h       Right ascension, equinox J2000.0 (hours)
 21- 22  I2    m       Right ascension, equinox J2000.0 (minutes)
 24- 28  F5.2  s       Right ascension, equinox J2000.0 (seconds)
     30  A1    ---     Declination, equinox J2000.0 (sign)
 31- 32  I2    deg     Declination, equinox J2000.0 (degrees)
 34- 35  I2    arcmin  Declination, equinox J2000.0 (arc minutes)
 37- 40  F4.1  arcsec  Declination, equinox J2000.0 (arc seconds)
 42- 46  A5    ---     Variability type
 48- 52  A5    ---     Subtype or secondary variability type
 55- 60  F6.3  mag     Intensity mean I-band magnitude
 62- 67  F6.3  mag     Intensity mean V-band magnitude
 69- 80  F     days    Period (if available)
 82- 86  F5.3  mag     I-band amplitude (for periodic variables)
 88- 99  F     days    Secondary period (if available)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------


Format of the files with photometry (phot/I/ID.dat and phot/V/ID.dat):
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
 Bytes  Format Units   Description
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
  1- 10  F10.5 days    Heliocentric Julian Day - 2450000
 12- 17  F6.3  mag     Magnitude
 19- 23  F5.3  mag     Uncertainty of magnitude
--------------------------------------------------------------------------


Finding charts are gzipped PostScript images. These are 60"x60" subframes
of the I-band reference frames centered on the star. White cross marks the
star. North is up and East to the left.


Any presentation of the scientific analysis or usage of the data from this
catalog should include the appropriate reference(s) to OGLE paper(s).

